{
  "schema": "openstitch-compat/1",
  "id": "spiral-ellipse40x30",
  "area": "stitches",
  "title": "Spiral Stitch: Circle/Ellipse, round 5",
  "description": "PE-DESIGN 11.50's Spiral Stitch: the outline offset a row (1 / density) inwards per turn. Round 5 settles the winding and the end: from a start point on an outline vertex (circle, ellipse, triangle corner) the spiral turns counter-clockwise and ends in the middle; from a start point inside an edge (a rectangle's bottom middle) it runs clockwise to the next corner, spirals from there and, after a trim, returns to that corner and runs back to the start. PE: starts at the bottom-middle (0,+14.8) and ends at the centre; runs right (counter-clockwise).",
